    "head_branch": "feature/spec-39-step-10c-i-threads-guard",
    "head_commit_message": "feat(sim): a unit-count threshold for threads, checked both ways in CI (spec 39 step 10c-i)\n\nThe tick's `threaded: bool` becomes `Threads` (One, Pool from 4,096 units, Always),\nand parting asks it with its bodies' count, so small battles stay on one thread.\nThe tools take threaded=true|false|always. CI's sim-checks takes each digest set,\nevery trial scenario and the fatigue trials with threaded=false and threaded=always\nand requires them equal to the default's. The spec records 10c's split (#730).\n\nNo outcome changes: parting's result doesn't depend on the pool.\n\nRefs #557. Closes #730.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi5cY9Riqyqasb22qUb",
